.TH "WSLNOTIFY" "1" "DATEPLACEHOLDER" "VERSIONPLACEHOLDER" "WSL Utilities User Manual"
.SH NAME
.B wslnotify
- Component of WSL Utilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wslnotify
.RB [ OPTIONS ]
.B TEXT
.RI [ TEXT ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Send a Windows toast notification from WSL. TEXT and all remaining words become the body of the toast; the first, bold line defaults to WSL and can be overridden with \fB--title\fR. The toast is shown under the Windows PowerShell app identity, so it lands in the Windows Action Center; Windows notification settings can suppress it. Use \fB--\fR before text beginning with a dash.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a simple help.
.TP
.B -v, --version
Print current version.
.TP
.B -t, --title \fITITLE\fR
Set the first, bold line of the toast. Defaults to WSL.
